imx678 — the IMX678 sensor driver of the black YIZHAN 4K camera (SigmaStar SSC8836 / Mercury6), in place of its stock
imx678_MIPI.ko

Licence: MIT No Attribution (../../LICENSE) or, at your choice, the GNU General Public License version 2 (../COPYING).

imx678.c, modes.py and Kbuild are made from OpenMicroCam's GC8613 driver (../gc8613); mhal_sensor.h is that driver's.
The register names follow the sensor's public Linux driver; none of its text is carried.

The register values in tables/ are facts about the sensor, in our own form:
- tables/vendor.txt: as the camera's stock sensor driver programs the sensor, read from that module of the camera's
  flash; no text of its maker is carried.
modes.py builds every mode's table from it and our changes to it; its output, modes.h, is made at build time.
